The saved temp-asset bootstrap gap is closed for the current UE 5.6.1 target: empty systems, empty emitters, visible sprite systems, conservative stock presets, and project-authored source-template seeds can all be created under `/Game/_MCP_Temp/NiagaraGenerated/` with compile/dependency checks. UE 5.6 graph-menu actions can now also be enumerated, transiently materialized for pin inspection, and used by a guarded ghost-only recipe writer. Unrestricted graph synthesis, source-asset Custom HLSL replacement, promotion policy outside temp, and visual quality authoring remain separate reviewed boundaries.

### `inspect_niagara_graph_actions` and guarded graph recipes

Status: implemented and live-validated against UE 5.6.1.

- `UEdGraphSchema_Niagara::GetGraphActions` is exported and provides the same native operation, conversion, selection, reroute, and function-call templates used by the Niagara graph menu.
- `FNiagaraSchemaAction_NewNode::SpawnNodeFromTemplate` can materialize a duplicated template into a transient preview graph, exposing the real pin surface without dirtying the asset.
- `UNiagaraGraph::NotifyGraphNeedsRecompile` is declared in a public header but is not exported from the installed engine DLL. Plugin callers must not link against it. The available compile route is `UNiagaraSystem::RequestCompile(false)` plus an explicit completion wait and diagnostic readback; force rebuild is deliberately avoided because it rotates rebuild/change IDs and would invalidate the mutation proof.
- The `UNiagaraGraph::FindOutputNodes` overloads and static final-node `BuildTraversal` overload needed by this reference proof are also declared without `NIAGARAEDITOR_API` in UE 5.6.1, so an external plugin cannot safely link them. The bridge therefore performs a conservative manual traversal: enumerate enabled output nodes, walk only enabled nodes through incoming links, and require a direct function-call reference to the selected Scratch Pad. `NiagaraNodeStaticSwitch`, `NiagaraNodeUsageSelector`, `NiagaraNodeSimTargetSelector`, and `NiagaraNodeSelect` are compile-time selector barriers; encountering one makes the scan incomplete and rejects the candidate rather than guessing the active branch.
- Generic numeric operation pins do not become typed merely because a literal default string is assigned. The water damping ghost test first failed with unresolved Clamp Min/Max pins, rolled back, then passed after the constants were authored as native `Make float` conversion nodes.
- The guarded writer accepts only generated systems under `/Game/_MCP_Temp/NiagaraGenerated`, requires an exact Custom HLSL body hash, and rejects an unreferenced, indirect-only, or selector-obscured Scratch Pad before mutation. UE 5.6 standalone Scratch Pad compilation can report false errors when emitter/system stack context is absent, so validation uses the real owning-system/caller context. Before both the pre-removal and final non-force compile, every caller's pending `ComputedId` must differ from baseline; after compile, both `CachedId` and `ComputedId` must match that captured pending ID while the caller remains clean and `UpToDate`.
- Dependency auditing runs before mutation and is repeated against the final native graph immediately before save. The final pass uses a non-mutating save-contract archive with an explicit read-only weak-reference pass and covers function calls, serialized node hard/soft/weak object and type references, pin type/default references, selected-function transitive dependencies, and direct system dependencies; incomplete traversal or an MCP-only reference rejects the result.
- Post-mutation failure performs best-effort structural restoration and a non-force recovery compile, but it is not a clean/full rollback. Even if node membership/order, Custom HLSL, links, graph fingerprint, and references are visibly restored, serialized `ChangeId`, `ForceRebuildId`, and traversal-cache IDs cannot be proven identical to disk. The ghost package therefore remains dirty, reports `rollback_verified=false`, `requires_package_reload=true`, `undo_recovery_unproven=true`, and `do_not_retry=true`. Reloading the exact package is the only supported recovery; Undo alone is not claimed safe, and the package must not be saved or retried before reload.
- The live harness now guards all recipe dispatches, including both dry runs, before transport begins. Malformed envelopes, request/response mode mismatches, and non-string status values remain fail-closed; independent graph or dirty-package evidence can restore the exact reload obligation even after a nominal no-mutation response. A saved disk-hash divergence is a different terminal state and requires a known-good manual restore instead of reloading the changed bytes.
- The per-phase timeout is normalized to a finite 1-60 seconds in both the Python payload and bridge, and the transport deadline covers all four possible compile waits (baseline, pre-removal, final, and recovery) plus margin. A socket/transport failure after dispatch is an indeterminate write outcome and is reported with mutation/save state unknown plus a reload-before-inspection contract rather than as a retryable generic failure.
- Ghost source-template creation follows the same fail-closed boundary: after promotion dispatch, any exception or missing/incomplete response aborts the whole run, claims the exact target for offline cleanup even if no package segment is visible yet, and requires exact-package reload/closed-editor cleanup before another mutation. Offline cleanup probes both GUI and commandlet editor processes, treats probe failure as unknown, and discovers all six recognized package segments even when `.uasset` is absent.
- The 2026-07-20 five-system ghost run inventoried 37 Custom HLSL nodes. Exactly 1 Water candidate reached and passed the guarded native-node conversion path; 36 remained unsupported and unchanged: 32 complex candidates plus 4 unreferenced Scratch Pads. The run kept every source package hash unchanged.
- The 2026-07-21 stability rerun retained the same 37/1/36 inventory contract, added an exact final editor-dirty gate across all five sources and five ghosts, and required every compact creation dependency audit to contain integer-zero forbidden/temp counts plus a typed dependency list. Promotion responses are now bound to the requested source/target paths and cross-check the post-promotion audit before a success can be admitted.

## Learning Commands

These commands should be read-only from a content perspective. They may create transient objects under `GetTransientPackage()` but must not save packages or dirty project content.

### `inspect_niagara_factory_bootstrap_defaults`

Status: implemented in the local MCP C++ bridge.

Parameters:

- `kind`: `"all" | "system" | "emitter" | "empty_emitter" | "basic_sprite_emitter"`
- `create_default_system_nodes`: bool, default `true`
- `add_default_modules_and_renderers`: bool, default `false`, used only with `kind="emitter"`
- `include_pins`: bool, default `false`
- `max_function_calls`: int, default `80`

Behavior:

- Create transient Niagara objects with the same factory static initializer paths.
- Inspect the resulting graph/script/output/module/renderer structure.
- Return a payload compatible with a compact `analyze_niagara_system` style response where possible.
- Never save, compile source assets, or register persistent asset registry entries.

Return fields:

- `kind`
- `transient_only=true`
- `saved=false`
- `compile_requested=false`
- `asset_registry_registered=false`
- `system`
- `emitters`

Use:

- Establish the expected UE 5.6.1 default structure without generating project content.
- Compare future generated assets against the engine default.

### `compare_niagara_system_bootstrap`

Parameters:

- `system_path`
- `baseline_kind`: `"empty_system" | "basic_sprite_system"`
- `include_graph=true`

Behavior:

- Inspect an existing Niagara System.
- Compare high-level counts and required defaults against the transient factory baseline.
- Do not mutate assets.

Return fields:

- `matches_baseline`
- `missing_outputs`
- `extra_emitters`
- `missing_default_modules`
- `renderer_diff`
- `compile_status`

Use:

- Validate manually created samples and later MCP-generated samples.

## Proposed Creation Commands

Creation commands should be implemented only after the transient learning command proves the baseline structure.

### `create_empty_niagara_system`

Status: implemented in the local MCP C++ bridge.

Parameters:

- `target_system_path`
- `overwrite_existing=false`
- `create_default_system_nodes=true`
- `save=true`
- `request_compile=true`

Safety:

- Refuse targets outside `/Game/_MCP_Temp/NiagaraGenerated/` unless `allow_non_temp_path=true` is explicitly supplied for the current call.
- Reject any target path containing `/Script/UnrealMCP`, `/UnrealMCP`, `UnrealMCP`, `MCPUnreal`, or `mcp_unreal`.
- No generated asset should reference the UnrealMCP plugin.
- The implemented first pass rejects overwrite attempts even when `overwrite_existing=true` is supplied.

Implementation:

- Use `AssetTools.CreateAsset` with a transient `UNiagaraSystemFactoryNew` whose `SystemToCopy` is null and `EmittersToAddToNewSystem` is empty.
- Let the factory initialize the system graph, assign default effect type, and request compile.
- Optionally wait/read compile status, save with the local direct save helper, then run dependency audit.

### `create_empty_niagara_emitter`

Status: implemented in the local MCP C++ bridge.

Parameters:

- `target_emitter_path`
- `add_default_modules_and_renderers=false`
- `overwrite_existing=false`
- `save=true`

Implementation:

- Use `AssetTools.CreateAsset` with a transient `UNiagaraEmitterFactoryNew`.
- Set `EmitterToCopy=nullptr`, `bUseInheritance=false`, and `bAddDefaultModulesAndRenderersToEmptyEmitter=false` for the real empty-emitter command.
- Allow `add_default_modules_and_renderers=true` only when the caller intentionally wants the editor's basic sprite emitter baseline.
- Save only generated/temp content by default.

### `create_basic_sprite_niagara_system`

Status: implemented in the local MCP C++ bridge.

Parameters:

- `target_system_path`
- `emitter_name="Emitter"`
- `material_path=""`
- `save=true`
- `wait_for_completion=true`

Implementation:

- Create a transient `UNiagaraEmitter` under `GetTransientPackage()`.
- Initialize it with `UNiagaraEmitterFactoryNew::InitializeEmitter(Emitter, true)`, set the desired unique emitter name, and set `Emitter->bIsInheritable=false`.
- Use `AssetTools.CreateAsset` with a transient `UNiagaraSystemFactoryNew` whose `EmittersToAddToNewSystem` contains that transient emitter version.
- Let `UNiagaraSystemFactoryNew::FactoryCreateNew` call `InitializeSystem`, `FNiagaraEditorUtilities::AddEmitterToSystem`, default effect-type assignment, and `RequestCompile(false)`.
- Verify that the owned emitter's `VersionedParent` and `VersionedParentAtLastMerge` are empty after creation.
- Save only the Niagara System in the first pass; do not create an auxiliary emitter asset unless a debug flag is added later.

### `create_sprite_niagara_preset_system`

Status: implemented in the local MCP C++ bridge.

Parameters:

- `target_system_path`
- `preset="basic"` (`basic`, `rain`, `snow`, `dust`, `sparks`)
- `emitter_name="Emitter"`
- `material_path=""`
- optional overrides: `spawn_rate`, `velocity`, `alignment`, `facing_mode`, `sub_image_size`, `fixed_bounds_min`, `fixed_bounds_max`, `local_space`, `add_spawn_box_location`, `spawn_box_size`, `spawn_box_offset`
- optional InitializeParticle overrides: `sprite_size`, `lifetime`
- optional weather-detail toggle: `add_weather_detail_modules`
- optional project weather material toggle: `use_project_weather_materials`
- `save=true`
- `wait_for_completion=true`

Implementation:

- Call the basic sprite creation path with `save=false` and `wait_for_completion=false`.
- Use `set_niagara_module_inputs_batch` internally with `save=false` and `request_compile=false` to tune the existing factory `SpawnRate.SpawnRate` and `AddVelocity.Velocity` RapidIteration inputs.
- For rain/snow by default, use `add_niagara_stock_module_to_stack` internally to insert `/Niagara/Modules/Spawn/Location/BoxLocation.BoxLocation`, then use `set_niagara_module_inputs_batch` to set `Box Size` and `Box Offset`.
- For rain/snow by default, update existing InitializeParticle RapidIteration parameters whose names contain `.SetVariables_` and end with `.Particles.SpriteSize` / `.Particles.Lifetime`. Verified UE 5.6.1 defaults are set through exact parameter suffixes rather than normal module-input lookup.
- For rain/snow by default, insert stock update modules `Drag`, `GravityForce`, `CurlNoiseForce`, `WindForce`, `ScaleColor`, and `ScaleSpriteSize`, then set their existing RapidIteration inputs.
- If `use_project_weather_materials=true` and `material_path` is empty, apply project-owned rain/snow particle materials from `/Game/MCPWeather`. This is opt-in because it creates a project-content dependency; it does not create an UnrealMCP/plugin dependency.
- Use the existing sprite renderer settings, fixed-bounds, and local-space handlers with `save=false` and `request_compile=false`.
- Request compile once, optionally wait, save once through the direct Niagara package-save helper, then return the same dependency audit and parent-reference checks as the basic creation command.
- Current presets are safe seed systems, not full weather/FX solvers; randomized variation, collision, camera-following, material-specific textures, and burst shaping remain later authoring work.

