- 2026-06-29 project-material opt-in smoke passed with `use_project_weather_materials=true`: rain applied `/Game/MCPWeather/FX/Rain/Materials/M_MCPWeather_Rain_Particle.M_MCPWeather_Rain_Particle`, snow applied `/Game/MCPWeather/FX/Snow/Materials/M_MCPWeather_Snow_Particle.M_MCPWeather_Snow_Particle`, and `inspect_niagara_renderers` confirmed each sprite renderer's `primary_material` and `used_materials`. Live compile remained at 0 errors/0 warnings, and current-map PNG evidence was written to `Saved/MCP/NiagaraReviews/project_materials_v1_current_map/`. Visual review confirms the option fixes material selection, while remaining quality work is preview framing/spawn density/volume behavior rather than plugin dependency or renderer material binding.
- 2026-06-29 preview framing pass added explicit camera controls to `capture_niagara_preview_lab_view`, `preview_niagara_system_in_preview_lab`, and `sample_niagara_system_in_preview_lab`: `auto_frame`, `camera_location`, `camera_rotation`, and `camera_fov`. Defaults remain auto-framed. Manual camera mode was verified against generated rain/snow project-material seed assets at `Saved/MCP/NiagaraReviews/manual_camera_safe_v1/` with `camera_mode="manual_camera_override"` and `map_dirty_after_preview=false`.
- 2026-06-29 preview override pass added `user_parameter_overrides` to `preview_niagara_system_in_preview_lab` and `sample_niagara_system_in_preview_lab`. Overrides are applied only to the transient preview `UNiagaraComponent` before activation, accept names with or without the `User.` namespace, and support bool/float/int/vector/color JSON values. This is intended for visual review of camera-following systems such as MCPWeather Snow where stronger `Amount` or custom camera values are useful, without mutating or saving the source Niagara System.
- 2026-06-29 preview asset-swap policy pass added `preserve_override_parameters=true` by default to the Python wrappers and native Preview Lab commands for `preview_niagara_system_in_preview_lab` and `sample_niagara_system_in_preview_lab`. The native command now calls `UNiagaraComponent::SetAsset(NiagaraSystem, !preserve_override_parameters)`. Keep this default for Blueprint/component swap parity; set it false only for A/B reset-path diagnostics.
- 2026-06-29 BP-manager Snow preview pass added `Python/scripts/analysis/preview_mcpweather_manager_source_template.py`. The script spawns a transient `/Game/MCPWeather/BP_MCPWeatherManager`, swaps `RainFX`/`SnowFX` to source or promoted systems, calls `SetWeather`/`EditorPreviewTick`, captures source/promoted viewport frames, and composes contact sheet/MP4 evidence. The first dense Snow run wrote visible source/promoted evidence under `Saved/MCP/NiagaraReviews/20260629_bp_manager_snow_source_template_v1/`, but a repeated dense rerun hit a UE 5.6.1 D3D12 out-of-video-memory fatal in Niagara rendering. Keep default boosts conservative, avoid repeated high-density Snow preview runs in one editor session, and restart the editor between dense visual passes.
- 2026-06-29 BP-manager preview stabilization lowered the default Snow/Rain preview boosts, hides and disables non-target Niagara components, attempts per-variant garbage collection, and releases viewport realtime after capture. Conservative Snow smoke `20260629_bp_manager_snow_stable_v2` completed without new Fatal/OOM/Python errors, cleared dirty flags back to zero, and wrote visible source/promoted contact sheet and MP4 evidence under `Saved/MCP/NiagaraReviews/20260629_bp_manager_snow_stable_v2/`.
- 2026-06-29 BP-manager Rain visual pass added per-run source/promoted path overrides, full-size contact sheets, transient fixed bounds on the preview Niagara component, dual `set_variable_*`/`set_niagara_variable_*` component setters, and a pre-swap `SetWeather`/`EditorPreviewTick` initialization attempt. Early Rain captures such as `20260629_bp_manager_rain_stable_v5` and `20260629_bp_manager_rain_stable_v7` completed and wrote MP4/contact-sheet evidence, but promoted Rain was much lower density than source Rain when simply swapped into `BP_MCPWeatherManager.RainFX`, despite source/promoted Rain matching 536/536 RapidIteration values, renderer summaries, user defaults, and read-only compile status.
- 2026-06-29 BP-manager Rain root-cause pass traced the mismatch to `UNiagaraComponent::SetAsset` editor behavior in UE 5.6.1. The default `SetAsset(system)` path resets `OverrideParameters` and `InstanceParameterOverrides` before synchronization, while `SetAsset(system, false)` preserves the BP component's existing override state during a promoted-system swap. `Python/scripts/analysis/preview_mcpweather_manager_source_template.py` now defaults to `--preserve-override-parameters`, logs `target_asset_swaps`, and exposes `--no-preserve-override-parameters` plus `--force-asset-rebind` for A/B checks. Evidence: `20260629_bp_manager_rain_preserve_override_v1` shows promoted Rain density matching source after warm-up; `20260629_bp_manager_rain_no_preserve_v1` reproduces the low/blank promoted Rain path. For BP-manager previews or runtime authoring tests, swap Niagara systems with override preservation; no C++ extension is required for this specific preview parity issue unless we later need deeper parameter-store readback/copy APIs.
- 2026-06-29 follow-up BP-manager Rain API-policy pass shows the above is necessary but not sufficient as a final visual proof. After the native Preview Lab API gained `preserve_override_parameters`, `20260629_bp_manager_rain_api_policy_v1` and `20260629_bp_manager_rain_promoted_only_probe_v1` still showed promoted Rain as low/blank in repeat BP-manager actor sessions, while the source-template RI/dependency audits continued to pass. Current conclusion: keep override preservation as the correct default SetAsset policy, but treat BP-manager Rain parity as a separate component-template/runtime-initialization problem. The next deeper step is C++ readback/copy support for `UNiagaraComponent` override/instance parameter state or a dedicated BP-manager preview harness that runs each variant in a fresh editor session.
- 2026-06-29 BP-manager Rain runtime-state pass narrowed the repeat blank to preview timing, not a broken promoted Niagara asset. The native `inspect_niagara_component_runtime_state` command now reads live `FNiagaraSystemInstance`/`FNiagaraEmitterInstance` counters without saving or compiling. Early promoted Rain attempts could report an active component but no system instance while the generated system was still compiling; after compile readiness, promoted Rain reported 7 active emitters and GPU particle counts but short captures could still look blank. A longer promoted-only run, `20260630_bp_manager_rain_promoted_long_after_compile_v1`, reached runtime age ~7.27s with 6 active GPU emitters and visible rain in `promoted_023.png`. The BP-manager preview harness now waits for Niagara compile readiness before setup and defaults promoted variants to an extra 240 post-setup settle frames, recording both `compile_ready` and `settle` in `preview_report.json`.
- 2026-06-30 BP-manager visual-review automation pass added per-frame image heuristics to `preview_mcpweather_manager_source_template.py`. The report now includes `frame_analysis` per variant and a top-level `frame_analysis_summary`. Rain uses a thin vertical-line candidate score, Snow uses bright neutral particle candidates, and consecutive-frame motion is recorded as a secondary signal. `--require-frame-analysis-pass` can turn the heuristic into a failing check, while the default remains evidence-only so human visual review can still arbitrate edge cases.
