## Remaining Questions

- Whether `UNiagaraSystemFactoryNew::InitializeSystem(System, false)` is useful for any diagnostic path. The editor path uses `true`, so `false` should remain out of the public authoring path unless a clear engine-source reason appears.
- Whether promotion should grow beyond first-pass duplication. Current implementation is intentionally conservative: dry-run by default, no overwrite, generated-temp source by default, non-temp target by default, and post-promotion dependency audit. Bulk promotion, overwrite/update, redirector handling, and source cleanup remain future reviewed work; the overwrite/update preflight contract now requires backup/restore, redirector/fixup, post-write audit, and plugin-independence evidence before that boundary can open.
- How far to automate broad Scratch Pad graph synthesis. Current support can inspect, duplicate, insert, and narrowly edit/link selected pins; arbitrary graph generation still needs more engine-source study and stricter graph-shape validation.
- Which preview route is safest for camera-following weather volumes. Current recommendation is manual preview camera controls or source-template copies; compact/local-space public preset changes are not promoted after the UE 5.6.1 worker assertion observed in preview.
